  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GHRUG Project: NIHR134717 - NIHR Global Health Research Group on Establishing Regional Hubs for Genomic Surveillance in West Africa, at the Wellcome Sanger Institute</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our goal is to expand capacity for genomic surveillance of malaria parasites and mosquito vectors in
West Africa, and to generate essential information required for National Malaria Control Programmes
(NMCPs) to plan sustainable interventions. Leveraging previous achievements in capacity building in
The Gambia and Ghana, we aim to establish regional sequencing hubs that will provide NMCPs with
timely, actionable genomic surveillance data.</narrative>
  </description>
